Theorem TF-5a: ApplyIndirect transfer produces CONSERVATIVE

  Preconditions:
    - Instruction is `ApplyIndirect { dst, closure, args }` per
      Annex E §AIMS TF-5a + Appendix A row 8
    - Closures have NO `MemoryContract` — closure environment captures
      heterogeneous state across call sites; no whole-program SCC fixpoint
      can derive a single contract per closure
    - CONSERVATIVE per TF-5 definition (same value)

  Soundness property:
    transfer_tf5a(ApplyIndirect { _, _, _ }) = CONSERVATIVE.
    L-6 layer (b) monotonicity: f(_) = CONSERVATIVE constant function;
    trivially monotone per L-4 reflexivity.

  Proof obligation:
    Discharge identical in shape to TF-5 Part (c) — TF-5a is a constant
    function emitting the same CONSERVATIVE value.

    Two-part discharge:
      (a) Output parity with TF-5 — verify transfer_tf5a() output matches
          CONSERVATIVE byte-for-byte across all 7 per-dimension carriers.
      (b) L-6 layer (b) monotonicity — constant-function check identical
          to TF-5: f(_) = CONSERVATIVE is reflexively monotone.

    Part (a) — CONSERVATIVE-parity check:
      transfer_tf5a() = CONSERVATIVE = (Owned, Unrestricted, Many,
      MaybeShared, Unknown, NonReusable, ALL = 0b111). Same value as TF-5
      per Appendix A rows 6 + 8 (both TF-5 and TF-5a emit CONSERVATIVE).
      Engine verifies the equality byte-for-byte against the canonical
      conservative() helper in section_04.rs.

    Part (b) — constant-function monotonicity:
      Identical to TF-5 Part (c) — f(_) = CONSERVATIVE is constant;
      CONSERVATIVE ≤ CONSERVATIVE by L-4 reflexivity on each dimension's
      carrier; product-order componentwise lift gives f(a) ≤ f(b).

    Rationale for separate TF rule (per Annex E §AIMS TF-5a):
      ApplyIndirect is distinct from Apply at the instruction-set level
      (ApplyIndirect carries a `closure: ArcVarId` operand vs Apply's
      `func: FnId`); the transfer function is identical because both lack
      a known contract. TF-5a exists to make the lack-of-contract handling
      explicit in the rule set vs reusing TF-5 ambiguously.

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) constant-function discharge per
        section_04::verify_tf5a_applyindirect_conservative)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix A row 8 forward-transfer column
        verification + CONSERVATIVE-parity check per
        section_04::verify_tf5a_applyindirect_conservative)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; ApplyIndirect emits
        CONSERVATIVE, never refine())

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-5a via Appendix A row 8 CONSERVATIVE-parity check + constant-function monotonicity
